   235	## Gate results
   236	
   237	- Gate A — PASS.  The exact source body executes.  Extensions are pure
   238	  definitions/derived lemmas except for the explicitly trusted fixed float
   239	  hook wrapper.  Equations have complete guarded coverage, overlaps agree,
   240	  recursive summaries descend, a satisfiable witness exists, the wrong
   241	  result is rejected, and a material body mutation is rejected.
   242	- Gate B — PASS.  The four symbolic entry claims cover arbitrary finite
   243	  nonempty numeric lists (including all int/bool/float mixtures) and arbitrary
   244	  finite nonempty string lists, which is the full domain on which the supplied
   245	  MPY `max` fold defines ordering.  The implementation directly calls Python's
   246	  `max`, and the formal summaries implement strict replacement with first-tie
   247	  retention.  Float conclusions are conditional on the supplied fixed
   248	  primitives, not on a candidate-added assumption.
   249	- Gate C — PASS.  The trust ledger is explicit; every reported test and
   250	  mutation has an artifact, exact command, scope, oracle, and actual result.
   251	  Formal, conditional, empirical, and excluded conclusions are separated.
